Modifications made to the upstream work
---------------------------------------

Documentation and skill definitions (SKILL.md, references/):

  * The 14 upstream skills were consolidated into one router skill. Top-level
    skills became references/mode-*.md; the four phase skills became
    references/phase-*.md. Their frontmatter was converted to HTML comments.
  * All reference paths were flattened into a single references/ namespace.
  * <plugin_dir> / <plugin-root> were replaced with $CXSEC_HOME.
  * All 143 upstream MCP tool references were converted to file operations. The
    mapping is documented in references/workbench-file-protocol.md; discovery,
    validation and attack-path state moved to candidates.jsonl plus per-candidate
    candidate_ledger.jsonl receipts.
  * Codex app links were replaced with instructions to verify that a connected
    MCP server exposes the required tools.
  * Product branding was removed from prose so mode selection does not depend on
    an absent product.
  * references/hard-rules.md corresponds to upstream references/scan-prologue.md
    (previously references/shared-hard-rules.md), edited to cover repository scans
    alongside diff and deep scans and to replace upstream's desktop-app,
    handoff-token and MCP-ownership machinery with the file protocol.
  * references/core-scan.md is upstream references/core-scan.md, the audit engine
    that replaced the four-phase pipeline for repository scans in 0.1.16+. Its
    checkpointing, which upstream performs through record_codex_security_scan_draft,
    is mapped to checkpoint files under <scan_dir>.
  * references/mode-deep-scan.md replaces upstream's MCP deep-scan coordinator
    with locally run Agent rounds, each performing the complete core-scan audit,
    followed by the same semantic reduction upstream's coordinator performs.
  * references/threat-model.md is upstream references/threat-model.md, which
    replaced skills/threat-model/references/threat-model-guidance.md.
  * references/mode-patch-risk.md and references/risk-rubric.md are upstream
    skills/assess-patch-risk, added in 0.1.16+.

Runtime layout (runtime/):

  * skills/assess-patch-risk/scripts/validate_patch_risk_assessment.py is
    vendored at its upstream depth rather than flattened into scripts/, because
    it resolves the plugin root as parents[3].

Runtime code (runtime/):

  * assets/0001-rebrand-sarif-output.patch renames five cosmetic SARIF branding
    sites in scripts/finalize_scan_contract.py: tool.driver.name, the
    partialFingerprints namespace, and three run.properties keys. Generated SARIF
    is attributed to cxsec-security.
  * No other functional change. Canonical wire literals (codex-security.*
    documentTypes, the codex-security/v1 fingerprint algorithm, and the
    codex-security-snapshot/v1 digest prefix) are deliberately unchanged so that
    genuine upstream artifacts remain ingestible.

